+- **Distinct accessible names.** On a Polaris page, two interactive elements
+  (links, buttons, `summary` disclosures and form controls) whose targets or
+  controlled regions differ SHALL have different accessible names, as the
+  browser computes them.
+  - A link's target is its resolved `href`; a `summary`'s controlled region
+    is its `details` element; a button's or form control's is the element
+    its `aria-controls` names, or the control itself when it names none.
+  - The interactive population is every link with an `href`, button,
+    `summary` and form control in the document after load, including those
+    inside a closed `details`, and excluding those hidden by the `hidden`
+    attribute, `aria-hidden="true"` or a computed `display: none`.
+  - An element's visible label is its text content with each whitespace run
+    collapsed to one space and the ends trimmed. Where elements of that
+    population whose targets differ share one visible label on a page, each
+    of their accessible names SHALL begin with that visible label. Where
+    such an element's target is an exact-source route response, the words
+    after the label SHALL include the repository-relative path the machine
+    answer carries for the source that route serves (PWB-REQ-011's machine
+    recovery). These two rules bind no other element.
+  - Two elements with the same target may share a name.
+- **Heading order.** A Polaris page SHALL have exactly one level-1 heading,
+  and in document order no heading SHALL be more than one level deeper than
+  the heading before it.
+  - The heading population is every `h1` to `h6` element, at its own level,
+    and every element with `role="heading"`, at its `aria-level`, in the
+    document after load, including those inside a closed `details`, and
+    excluding those hidden by the `hidden` attribute, `aria-hidden="true"`
+    or a computed `display: none`.
+  - No heading in that population is exempt, including one Polaris renders
+    from Butlers-declared text.
